From d60160cbe568e2c3b846d38ee20ca5c78ddc0281 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:06:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-79: the artboard toolbar and the tag navigator,
 like WPF (0.79.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"所有基礎操作模式能跟WPF一樣方便" (EastSun 20260930), parts 5 and 9, from Microsoft's
"Create UIs with Visual Studio XAML Designer" / "WPF and Silverlight Designer
Overview":
- the design surface's bottom-left toolbar (WPF's artboard commands): zoom out /
  the zoom list (25 %..400 %, fit all, fit selection) / zoom in, fit all, fit
  selection, the snap grid (the designer's grid setting), snaplines on / off
  (kept across the page's redraws; off = a drag snaps to nothing and draws no
  red line). Its clicks are handled with the overlay's own events: the page
  never sees them (no selection change); hidden in operate mode.
- the tag navigator ("lets you move to any parent tag of the currently
  selected tag"): the Properties header shows the component's parents on the
  page (the form as 表單), each a click away -- the panel posts selectId, the
  designer selects it; the DFM path is the tooltip.
- vscode_it: the Shift+F7 check waits on THAT page's designer (another open
  one may be the active designer a moment later) and reports what it saw.

Tests (all 4 layers pass): probe (the toolbar: 7+ buttons, + = 110 %, the list
has 9+ items, 50 % picked and the list closed, the label says 50 %, grid and
snaplines posted, snaplines shown off, the page's selection unchanged), panels
(表單 > Panel2 > spbSave, a click on Panel2 posts selectId Panel2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
